WEBVTT

00:00:02.993 --> 00:00:04.527
No, the painters canceled.

00:00:04.628 --> 00:00:06.096
- Uh-huh.
- True story.

00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:07.763
- Wow. -I don't know what is
the deal with these...

00:00:07.864 --> 00:00:09.232
- GRU: Morning, neighbors!
- Uh...

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:10.734
Hey there!

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.336
Still waiting on that invite,
Perry.

00:00:13.436 --> 00:00:14.604
- Uh...
- (gasps) Oh!

00:00:14.704 --> 00:00:16.772
- No. No. No, no.
- Yoo-hoo!

00:00:16.873 --> 00:00:18.508
- Patsy. (grunts)
- Oh, neighbors.

00:00:18.608 --> 00:00:20.510
- Oh, Patsy.
- Hi there.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.579
I'm Perry's wife Patsy.

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:23.747
Oh. I'm Blanche.

00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:25.382
And this is Chet.

00:00:25.482 --> 00:00:28.918
Hi. So I look over here,
and I see you, and... (laughs)

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:31.087
I have one of
my brilliant ideas.

00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:34.190
Perry needs a fourth
for tennis tomorrow.

00:00:34.291 --> 00:00:35.592
Oh, honey.

00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:37.093
(chuckles):
I... I don't know.

00:00:37.193 --> 00:00:39.763
He doesn't seem like
much of a tennis guy.

00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:41.064
Much of a tennis guy?

00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:42.866
I am too much of a tennis guy.

00:00:42.966 --> 00:00:44.768
I'm Mr. Tennis.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:48.004
It's my favorite
of all the sports games.

00:00:48.104 --> 00:00:50.974
With the racket and, uh,
with the balls.

00:00:51.074 --> 00:00:53.143
- So yellow and fuzzy.
- (Perry groans)

00:00:53.243 --> 00:00:55.111
- (Perry grunts)
- Oh, then we're all set.

00:00:55.211 --> 00:00:56.913
See you two at the club
tomorrow.

00:00:57.013 --> 00:00:58.948
(laughs)
Toodle-oo.

00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:01.384
Okay. Toodle-oo to you two, too.

00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:02.786
(chuckles)

00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:04.788
So, you-you play tennis?

00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:07.691
Yes, yes, I play tennis.

00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:09.993
I'm pretty fantastic, actually.

00:01:10.093 --> 00:01:12.395
Well, at least I was
at summer camp.

00:01:12.495 --> 00:01:13.630
Wow, that's great.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:14.831
Here you go.

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:16.666
- Mwah. Okay, bye.
- (Gru Jr. fussing)

00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:19.336
- (Gru chuckles nervously)
- Have fun.

00:01:20.403 --> 00:01:22.005
There you go.

00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:24.607
(groaning):
Okay.

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:26.976
- (grunts) Huh?
- (laughs)

00:01:28.445 --> 00:01:31.114
♪

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.086
What the... (yelps)

00:01:37.587 --> 00:01:39.356
(sighs)

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.359
♪

00:01:45.628 --> 00:01:47.997
(whirring)

00:01:51.401 --> 00:01:52.569
Gru.

00:01:52.669 --> 00:01:54.437
You can't hide from me, Gru.

00:01:54.537 --> 00:01:57.107
- (back cracks)
- Ay, my back is killing me.

00:01:57.207 --> 00:01:59.008
How long is this gonna take?

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:01.745
It will take
as long as it takes.

00:02:01.846 --> 00:02:04.481
Mark my words, Gru will not win.

00:02:04.581 --> 00:02:07.584
This won't be like
the ninth grade talent show.

00:02:07.684 --> 00:02:09.886
Ay, again with this.

00:02:09.986 --> 00:02:12.522
Yes, again.
It was a pivotal moment.

00:02:12.622 --> 00:02:14.424
Why can't you indulge me?

00:02:14.524 --> 00:02:16.793
(both groan)

00:02:16.893 --> 00:02:18.528
It was the night
of the big show.

00:02:18.628 --> 00:02:19.596
(Valentina scoffs)

00:02:20.497 --> 00:02:22.332
MAXIME:
<i>I had practiced for weeks,</i>

00:02:22.432 --> 00:02:25.935
<i>perfecting a number that would
blow my classmates away.</i>

00:02:26.035 --> 00:02:28.638
♪ Karma, karma, karma, karma,
karma chameleon... ♪

00:02:28.738 --> 00:02:30.740
<i>I was about to go on when...</i>

00:02:30.841 --> 00:02:32.242
- What?
<i>- I heard it.</i>

00:02:32.342 --> 00:02:34.978
- Wait. Oh.
- ("Karma Chameleon" playing)

00:02:36.146 --> 00:02:39.949
♪ Karma, karma, karma, karma,
karma chameleon... ♪

00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:42.752
MAXIME:
<i>There was that little jerk</i>

00:02:42.853 --> 00:02:44.187
<i>doing my big number.</i>

00:02:44.287 --> 00:02:47.123
GRU:
♪ You come and go...

00:02:47.858 --> 00:02:49.626
He ruined everything.

00:02:49.726 --> 00:02:50.927
I couldn't go on after him.

00:02:51.027 --> 00:02:52.762
I would've looked like a fool.

00:02:52.863 --> 00:02:54.731
Like I was copying him.

00:02:54.832 --> 00:02:56.933
Maybe it was just a coincidence.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.903
That was a very popular song.

00:02:59.002 --> 00:03:00.905
Oh, no, no, no, no. He knew.

00:03:01.004 --> 00:03:02.739
He did it on purpose.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.641
He reveled in humiliating me.

00:03:04.741 --> 00:03:06.176
- (alarm blaring)
- Huh?

00:03:06.276 --> 00:03:08.913
- What now?
- Ugh, we're low on fuel.

00:03:09.012 --> 00:03:10.513
It's always something.

00:03:10.613 --> 00:03:13.683
Look, I can never focus
on just being evil.

00:03:13.783 --> 00:03:15.485
(groans) Okay.

00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:17.320
Pull over.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.023
♪

00:03:21.524 --> 00:03:22.826
(wind whistling)

00:03:22.927 --> 00:03:25.128
(barking)

00:03:26.596 --> 00:03:28.264
(dog whimpers)

00:03:29.466 --> 00:03:30.901
(slurping)

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.368
(dog yelps)

00:03:36.306 --> 00:03:38.575
- (slurping bottom of cup)
- (dog grumbles)

00:03:38.675 --> 00:03:40.176
(coughing)

00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:44.514
♪

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.584
Okay, let's see.

00:03:47.684 --> 00:03:49.452
Regular unleaded.

00:03:49.552 --> 00:03:50.687
Ooh. Wow.

00:03:50.787 --> 00:03:52.155
It is expensive, no?

00:03:52.255 --> 00:03:55.992
Okay. Insert card
and remove rapidly.

00:03:56.092 --> 00:03:58.228
- "Card not read."
- (machine beeping)

00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:02.565
- Oh, come on.
- Did you pull it out rapidly?

00:04:02.665 --> 00:04:05.001
Yes, yes, very rapidly.

00:04:05.101 --> 00:04:07.938
- (grumbling)
- (machine beeping repeatedly)

00:04:08.037 --> 00:04:09.706
(prolonged beep)

00:04:09.806 --> 00:04:11.674
- (yells)
- (beeping stops)

00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:15.578
Ay, get me a slushy.
It's my cheat day.

00:04:15.678 --> 00:04:16.746
(entry bell jingles)

00:04:16.847 --> 00:04:20.717
Hey, you, your stupid machine
won't read my card.

00:04:20.817 --> 00:04:22.552
Did you remove it rapidly?

00:04:22.652 --> 00:04:23.753
- Yes.
- (sighs)

00:04:23.854 --> 00:04:26.022
Well, sometimes it's too rapid.

00:04:26.122 --> 00:04:28.157
You should probably try again.

00:04:28.258 --> 00:04:31.427
(groans)
I don't have time for this!

00:04:31.528 --> 00:04:33.062
(whimpers) Whoa!

00:04:33.162 --> 00:04:37.200
I'm trying to destroy
my archnemesis.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.303
Now, give me 900 gallons
on pump four, you idiot.

00:04:40.403 --> 00:04:43.039
(whimpers)
Please don't hurt me.

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:45.174
Oh, I'm not going to hurt you.

00:04:45.275 --> 00:04:46.743
- (chuckles)
- (weapon powering up)

00:04:46.844 --> 00:04:48.511
- Wha...
- (weapon blasts)

00:04:48.611 --> 00:04:51.381
- Ow! (grunting rapidly)
- (electrical crackling)

00:04:52.482 --> 00:04:53.851
(grunting)

00:04:53.951 --> 00:04:55.285
(groans, chatters)

00:04:55.385 --> 00:04:57.220
MAXIME:
Oh, look at you.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.857
(laughs)
Much better.

00:04:59.957 --> 00:05:01.758
Now, get me a purple slushy!

00:05:01.859 --> 00:05:03.359
(yelling, groaning)

00:05:03.459 --> 00:05:05.695
I'm not paying for that,
just so you know.

00:05:05.795 --> 00:05:06.864
So there. (laughs)

00:05:06.964 --> 00:05:08.264
I know I'm so bad.

00:05:08.364 --> 00:05:10.700
- (Maxime laughing)
- (grumbles)

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.268
(entry bell jingles)

00:05:13.871 --> 00:05:17.975
Hmm. Okay, why don't you guys
pick out a healthy cereal?

00:05:18.074 --> 00:05:21.411
(gasps) This was Lucky's
favorite cereal.

00:05:22.278 --> 00:05:25.515
You don't think
he'll forget me, do you?

00:05:25.615 --> 00:05:28.551
Oh, sweetheart,
that's impossible.

00:05:28.651 --> 00:05:31.354
You play with Lucky
and-and dress him up.

00:05:31.454 --> 00:05:33.323
And you guys have your podcast.

00:05:33.423 --> 00:05:37.061
There is no way in this world
he could ever forget

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.495
- his best friend.
- (laughs)

00:05:39.596 --> 00:05:41.497
Thanks, Mom.

00:05:41.598 --> 00:05:42.900
Oh, look it!

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.836
This one has extra marshmallows!

00:05:45.936 --> 00:05:47.403
Double Frosted Choco Clusters.

00:05:47.503 --> 00:05:49.974
- AGNES: Yeah.
- Yeah, let's go with those.

00:05:50.074 --> 00:05:51.875
All right, what else do we need?

00:05:51.976 --> 00:05:53.911
(gasping)

00:05:54.011 --> 00:05:55.545
Oh, no.

00:05:55.645 --> 00:05:58.247
Nobody see. Nobody notice.
Nobody notice.

00:05:58.348 --> 00:06:00.550
- (whimpering)
- (Agnes yelps)

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.819
- Whew.
- EDITH: What's wrong?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.153
Huh?

00:06:04.253 --> 00:06:06.023
Oh, nothing. Just, uh...

00:06:06.122 --> 00:06:08.892
ooh, stretching
before we hit the aisles.

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:12.195
Shopping is the number one
cause of pulled hamstrings.

00:06:12.295 --> 00:06:14.364
Probably didn't know that.

